// Explorer.t -- translations for Explorer's own strings.
//
// This file is *included as data*, not compiled: ExplorerLang.cpp does
//
//	#define TFILE <Explorer/Explorer.t>
//	#include <Core/t.h>
//
// and Core/t.h turns every T_() line here into a table entry. That is why the
// entries are bare braces-with-two-strings and not code: a line that does not
// parse as `T_("english") xxYY("translation")` is not a string to translate, it
// is a build failure, and the failure names the line.
//
// English is the *key*, not a translation: T_("Bookmarks") means "the word
// Bookmarks in the source". A string that is not in this file still works --
// t_() falls back to the key -- which is why a missing entry shows up as one
// English word in a Finnish window rather than as a crash.
//
// fiFI first because this is where the work is being done; the others are the
// ones the fork's other packages already carry for the same words. An empty
// translation is not "same as English": it is *no translation*, and
// t_() falls through to the key, so an entry left empty shows English rather
// than an empty label.

